        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "बुरो (buro) is a tadbhava, a word inherited and reshaped by sound change. It comes from bura, \"defective\", a form CDIAL reconstructs from its descendants. CDIAL gives no Marwari form in this entry (CDIAL 9289); the match is through Hindi burā and Gujarati būrũ. CDIAL sets it in a large group of \"defective\" words."
            }
          ]
        },
